      "live_backlinks": [
        "./tools/ci/ci-coverage.mjs:7:// \"gated by nothing\". See docs/archive/research/CAMPAIGN-2026-08.md.",
        "./js/track/scenery/city.js:751:          // re-measured \u2014 see docs/archive/research/CAMPAIGN-2026-08.md.",
        "./docs/research/STRUCTURE-REDECISION-2026-08.md:59:**Deciding evidence.** No new fact disturbs a doubly-recorded ruling (CLAUDE.md \"grandfathered \u2014 do not churn them\"; CAMPAIGN-2026-08.md:913 \"js/game rename NO-GO is final\"). The governing test \u2014 \"renaming is not restructuring: does it reduce a COUNT?\" \u2014 fails a 15-file rename outright: same 46 files, same contents. Each rename is a 5-point lockstep (git mv + index.html tag + manifest.cjs + sw.js precache + `?v`/version.json) under load-order.test.mjs, executed by parallel agent sessions \u2014 the exact unsynchronized-bulk-change shape the repo's post-mortems identify as its historical damage source \u2014 plus blame discontinuity on files whose headers carry safety contracts (`debrisworld.js` \"NEVER moves a game car\"). The genuinely confusable clusters (cam-tune/cam-tuner/tuner; lighting/light-store/light-presets) are all hyphenated already and handled by CLAUDE.md's disambiguation table. **Earliest rational reconsideration point:** after gen-manifest lands, when a rename becomes a one-field edit \u2014 and even then the payoff is cosmetic.",
        "./docs/research/STRUCTURE-REDECISION-2026-08.md:99:- **`docs/archive/research/CAMPAIGN-2026-08.md`:** no annotation needed \u2014 the R3 cut and the js/game rename NO-GO were both re-tested against fresh evidence and held."
      ]
    },
